course: dictionary
lesson: 102
title: Ade: a drink, an ending, a name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The letters a-d-e can mean different things, so look at the words around them to decide which meaning fits. Ade can be a drink, a word ending, or a name.
explain: Think of lemonade, a sweet drink made from fruit juice, water and sugar. Here -ade is part of the drink's name. Many other words end in -ade too, such as parade and escapade, so you can spot this ending in spelling lessons.
explain: Ade can also be a name. «When Ade goes off to play with the Year 6 lads, Sam and Jake stop moping.» Ade is a person here, because the children go off to play and stop moping. The capital letter and the story around it show you it is a name.
fact: Ade is a noun for a sweet drink made from fruit juice, water and sugar.
fact: Drinks with the -ade ending include lemonade, orangeade and limeade.
fact: -ade is a suffix, an ending added to the end of a word, as in parade, blockade and barricade.
fact: Ade is a short form of the names Adrian or Adeola.
fact: «Sam's friend Ade goes to Nigeria for a year and they write real letters.» A capital letter at the start of a word, in the middle of a sentence, is often a clue that it is a name.
exercise: «Ade's reply takes two months and has a stamp with a bird on it.» Is Ade a drink or a name here? | A sweet drink | *A name for a person | A word ending like -ade | A type of fruit
exercise: Which word in this list ends with the suffix -ade? | happy | green | table | *blockade
exercise: What is lemonade? | *A sweet drink made from fruit juice, water and sugar | A sour kind of soup | A kind of bread
test: What is a suffix like -ade? | A sweet drink made from fruit | *An ending added to the end of a word | A word that goes in front of another word | A word that means the same as another word
test: Ade is a short form of which names? | *Adrian and Adeola | Alice and Ahmed | Ava and Aiden | Adam and Ada
exam: In «Ade's reply takes two months and has a stamp with a bird on it», how do you know Ade is a name? | It is at the end of a word | It rhymes with lemonade | *It starts with a capital letter and acts like a person in the story | It means a sweet drink
